**Finding submitted: MISSING (critical) — no indemnification section in the Agreement.**

What I found:
- The numbering jumps from Section 19 (Warranties) straight to Section 21 (Limitation of Liability). There is no defence, indemnity or hold-harmless language anywhere in the document.
- Several clauses nevertheless presuppose an indemnity regime: Section 9.3 conditions our termination right on "the remedies required by Section 20.5" (a non-existent section), Section 19.4 preserves remedies for "indemnified claims", Section 21.3 carves "indemnification obligations" out of the liability cap as Excluded Claims, and Section 30.5 refers to "an indemnified party" and "vested indemnity rights".
- Net effect: we have no Vendor IP infringement or misconduct indemnity at all — the playbook walk-away outcome.

Redline (validated, preferred level): a new **Section 20 — INDEMNIFICATION** inserted after Section 19.5, comprising:
- 20.1 Vendor defence/indemnity for third-party IP infringement claims, Vendor's breach of Applicable Law, Vendor-caused unauthorized access to Customer Data, and Vendor's gross negligence or wilful misconduct (extending to Customer Affiliates);
- 20.2 a narrow reciprocal Customer indemnity limited to Customer-provided content and Customer's breach of Applicable Law, with an express statement that Customer has no other indemnity obligation;
- 20.3 standard procedure (prompt notice with prejudice qualifier, indemnitor control, cooperation at indemnitor's cost, no adverse settlement without consent);
- 20.4 customary IP exclusions (Customer modifications, combinations, Customer specifications);
- 20.5 infringement remedies (procure, modify, replace, else terminate and refund) — which also repairs the dangling cross-reference in Section 9.3.
